{"archetypes":[{"name":"rounds-root-inflight","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan adds inflight skip using _review_rounds_root but does not trace flushed larch-logs roots versus live implement_tmpdir round dirs that _current_round_dir still uses for liveness headers.","prompt_body":"Compare the planned _all_round_dirs_inflight guard in python/progress_report.py against how _render_step5 and _render_review_detail already pick rounds roots via _review_rounds_root and _current_round_dir. Exercise mixed states where larch-logs/implement/<run_id> holds completed or in-flight rounds while a newer round-N directory still lives directly under the implement tmpdir. Verify the inflight-only skip fires only when every round under the same root passed to the shared renderer lacks round-meta.json, and that skipping detail does not regress test_review_rounds_root_prefers_flushed_log_during_live_round behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-lint-precheck","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's assert_mermaid_valid contract depends on never calling python/cli.py lint mermaid-fences without a pre-existing mmdc, but python/lint_mermaid_fences.py can run npm ci when mmdc is missing.","prompt_body":"Audit the planned assert_mermaid_valid helper in scripts/test-render-review-phase-detail.sh against python/lint_mermaid_fences.py and python/test_lint_mermaid_fences.py behavior for missing mmdc, exit code 2, and zero-fence files. Confirm required-mode GITHUB_ACTIONS and LARCH_MERMAID_REQUIRED=1 paths cannot silently skip, while optional local mode prints exactly one SKIP breadcrumb and never creates mermaid-lint/node_modules or triggers npm ci from the harness itself. Check that every planned Gantt-producing fixture call site is covered and that --no-gantt cases remain excluded. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shard-topology-sync","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"CI Mermaid install is pinned to matrix shard 12 and Makefile test-harnesses-12, but scripts/render-review-phase-detail.md still documents shard test-harnesses-2 and the plan does not list that doc for correction.","prompt_body":"Cross-check the planned .github/workflows/ci.yaml shard-12 Node/npm/puppeteer conditionals against the existing lint-mermaid job install/cache/retry contract and the Makefile test-harnesses-12 target that runs test-render-review-phase-detail. Hunt for drift between harness docs (scripts/render-review-phase-detail.md, scripts/test-render-review-phase-detail.md, docs/linting.md) and actual shard registration, including stale shard numbers or missing edit-in-sync updates when CI gains a second Mermaid toolchain consumer. Confirm the plan's Makefile-sync comment is sufficient or identify missing doc edits. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
